  "units": [
    {
      "ancestors": [],
      "attributes": [
        {
          "doc_text": " Trait that indicates that this is a pointer or a wrapper for one,",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            44,
            113
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " where unsizing can be performed on the pointee.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            114,
            165
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            166,
            169
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " See the [DST coercion RFC][dst-coerce] and [the nomicon entry on coercion][nomicon-coerce]",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            170,
            264
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " for more details.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            265,
            286
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            287,
            290
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " For builtin pointer types, pointers to `T` will coerce to pointers to `U` if `T: Unsize<U>`",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            291,
            386
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " by converting from a thin pointer to a fat pointer.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            387,
            442
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            443,
            446
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " For custom types, the coercion here works by coercing `Foo<T>` to `Foo<U>`",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            447,
            525
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " provided an impl of `CoerceUnsized<Foo<U>> for Foo<T>` exists.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            526,
            592
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Such an impl can only be written if `Foo<T>` has only a single non-phantomdata",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            593,
            675
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " field involving `T`. If the type of that field is `Bar<T>`, an implementation",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            676,
            757
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " of `CoerceUnsized<Bar<U>> for Bar<T>` must exist. The coercion will work by",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            758,
            837
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " coercing the `Bar<T>` field into `Bar<U>` and filling in the rest of the fields",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            838,
            921
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " from `Foo<T>` to create a `Foo<U>`. This will effectively drill down to a pointer",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            922,
            1007
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " field and coerce that.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1008,
            1034
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1035,
            1038
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Generally, for smart pointers you will implement",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1039,
            1091
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " `CoerceUnsized<Ptr<U>> for Ptr<T> where T: Unsize<U>, U: ?Sized`, with an",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1092,
            1169
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " optional `?Sized` bound on `T` itself. For wrapper types that directly embed `T`",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1170,
            1254
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " like `Cell<T>` and `RefCell<T>`, you",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1255,
            1295
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " can directly implement `CoerceUnsized<Wrap<U>> for Wrap<T> where T: CoerceUnsized<U>`.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1296,
            1386
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " This will let coercions of types like `Cell<Box<T>>` work.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1387,
            1449
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1450,
            1453
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " [`Unsize`][unsize] is used to mark types which can be coerced to DSTs if behind",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1454,
            1537
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " pointers. It is implemented automatically by the compiler.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1538,
            1600
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1601,
            1604
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " [dst-coerce]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/blob/master/text/0982-dst-coercion.md",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1605,
            1694
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " [unsize]: crate::marker::Unsize",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1695,
            1730
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " [nomicon-coerce]: ../../nomicon/coercions.html",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1731,
            1781
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": null,
          "path": "unstable",
          "range": [
            1782,
            1838
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": null,
          "path": "lang",
          "range": [
            1839,
