    {
      "ancestors": [],
      "attributes": [
        {
          "doc_text": " `DispatchFromDyn` is used in the implementation of dyn-compatibility[^1] checks (specifically",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3461,
            3558
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " allowing arbitrary self types), to guarantee that a method's receiver type can be dispatched on.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3559,
            3659
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3660,
            3663
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Note: `DispatchFromDyn` was briefly named `CoerceSized` (and had a slightly different",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3664,
            3753
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " interpretation).",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3754,
            3774
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3775,
            3778
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Imagine we have a trait object `t` with type `&dyn Tr`, where `Tr` is some trait with a method",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3779,
            3877
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " `m` defined as `fn m(&self);`. When calling `t.m()`, the receiver `t` is a wide pointer, but an",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3878,
            3977
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " implementation of `m` will expect a narrow pointer as `&self` (a reference to the concrete",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3978,
            4072
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " type). The compiler must generate an implicit conversion from the trait object/wide pointer to",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4073,
            4171
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " the concrete reference/narrow pointer. Implementing `DispatchFromDyn` indicates that that",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4172,
            4265
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " conversion is allowed and thus that the type implementing `DispatchFromDyn` is safe to use as",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4266,
            4363
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " the self type in an dyn-compatible method. (in the above example, the compiler will require",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4364,
            4459
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " `DispatchFromDyn` is implemented for `&'a U`).",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4460,
            4510
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4511,
            4514
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " `DispatchFromDyn` does not specify the conversion from wide pointer to narrow pointer; the",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4515,
            4609
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " conversion is hard-wired into the compiler. For the conversion to work, the following",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4610,
            4699
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " properties must hold (i.e., it is only safe to implement `DispatchFromDyn` for types which have",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4700,
            4799
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " these properties, these are also checked by the compiler):",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4800,
            4862
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4863,
            4866
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " * EITHER `Self` and `T` are either both references or both raw pointers; in either case, with",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4867,
            4964
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "   the same mutability.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4965,
            4991
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " * OR, all of the following hold",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4992,
            5027
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "   - `Self` and `T` must have the same type constructor, and only vary in a single type parameter",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            5028,
            5128
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "     formal (the *coerced type*, e.g., `impl DispatchFromDyn<Rc<T>> for Rc<U>` is ok and the",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            5129,
            5224
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "     single type parameter (instantiated with `T` or `U`) is the coerced type,",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            5225,
            5306
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "     `impl DispatchFromDyn<Arc<T>> for Rc<U>` is not ok).",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            5307,
            5367
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "   - The definition for `Self` must be a struct.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            5368,
            5419
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "   - The definition for `Self` must not be `#[repr(packed)]` or `#[repr(C)]`.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            5420,
            5500
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "   - Other than one-aligned, zero-sized fields, the definition for `Self` must have exactly one",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            5501,
            5599
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "     field and that field's type must be the coerced type. Furthermore, `Self`'s field type must",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            5600,
            5699
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "     implement `DispatchFromDyn<F>` where `F` is the type of `T`'s field type.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            5700,
            5781
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            5782,
            5785
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " An example implementation of the trait:",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            5786,
            5829
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            5830,
            5833
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " ```",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            5834,
            5841
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " # #![feature(dispatch_from_dyn, unsize)]",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            5842,
            5886
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " # use std::{ops::DispatchFromDyn, marker::Unsize};",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            5887,
            5941
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " # struct Rc<T: ?Sized>(std::rc::Rc<T>);",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            5942,
            5985
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " impl<T: ?Sized, U: ?Sized> DispatchFromDyn<Rc<U>> for Rc<T>",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            5986,
            6049
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " where",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            6050,
            6059
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "     T: Unsize<U>,",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            6060,
            6081
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " {}",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            6082,
            6088
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " ```",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            6089,
            6096
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            6097,
            6100
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " [^1]: Formerly known as *object safety*.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            6101,
            6145
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": null,
          "path": "unstable",
